From: cl4ude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reject min_value=0.0, max_value=-0.0 in float draws

generate_float checked `min_value > max_value`, which is false for
0.0 and -0.0, so the draw went ahead. FloatChoice compares the bounds
sign-aware, so no float is in [0.0, -0.0]: simplest() found nothing
and the draw returned HEGEL_E_INTERNAL ("FloatChoice::simplest: no
valid float for this choice").

A caller that orders two drawn floats with `a < b ? a : b` hits this
whenever it draws -0.0 then 0.0. The Rust frontend already rejects
these bounds itself; C callers did not.

Compare the bounds with sign_aware_lte, as the Rust frontend does, so
the call returns HEGEL_E_INVALID_ARG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019ndjvpGmcVSSUGqdpJKe5V
---
 libhegel/RELEASE/float-signed-zero-bounds.md |  3 +++
 libhegel/src/native/draws/mod.rs             |  3 ++-
 libhegel/tests/c_abi_generate.rs             | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
